+// Package effectlog captures effect-shaped calls as replayable observations.
+//
+// It deliberately does not schedule work. Callers retain their ordinary Go
+// control flow and wrap only the external operation whose response must be
+// reproducible. A capture is keyed by a stable step definition, a semantic
+// request key, and an attempt number. Run, stage, operation, and attempt IDs
+// remain trace identity: they explain one execution without contaminating the
+// semantic request identity used for replay.
+package effectlog
